==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}}, from {{etyl|la|en}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}}, from {{etyl|he|en}} {{term|הֶבֶל||breath, vapor; vanity|tr=hével|lang=he}} or from {{etyl|akk|en}} {{term|tr=ablu|||son|lang=akk}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈeɪ.bəl/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|able}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# The son of [[Adam]] and [[Eve]] who was killed by his brother [[Cain]].
#* {{RQ:Authorized Version|Genesis|4|8}}:
#*: And Cain talked with '''Abel''' his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against '''Abel''' his brother, and slew him.
# {{given name|male|from=Hebrew}}.

